    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-12t,\\,y=-{t}^{3}+\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2}-6t,\\,-\\infty<t<\\infty.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
